00:28:35,860 --> 00:28:40,160
those formed by the breakdown of man-made infrastructure hidden under a bustling city.

348
00:28:41,540 --> 00:28:45,220
A common culprit is the collapse of a deteriorating sewer pipe.

349
00:28:45,520 --> 00:28:49,440
As far as sewer collapses, they're, of course, not a natural phenomenon,

350
00:28:49,580 --> 00:28:51,800
because of a man-made condition.

351
00:28:51,900 --> 00:28:55,480
But again, you have the similarity between those and the natural phenomenon

352
00:28:55,481 --> 00:28:59,120
because you have water that's basically carrying away soils.

353
00:29:00,580 --> 00:29:04,880
During the early 1900s, rapidly expanding cities around the country

354
00:29:04,881 --> 00:29:06,940
began building networks of sewer tunnels.

355
00:29:08,200 --> 00:29:11,820
Close to a century later, many of these aging tunnel-like pipes

356
00:29:11,821 --> 00:29:15,020
have begun to fail, sometimes with deadly consequences.

357
00:29:16,060 --> 00:29:18,940
The potential for this kind of thing can happen anywhere.

358
00:29:18,941 --> 00:29:24,020
And a lot of it just depends on how old these lines are and what may have been placed on top of them.

359
00:29:24,021 --> 00:29:28,940
Because the original designs probably never anticipated some of the conditions that they're exposed to now.

360
00:29:29,940 --> 00:29:38,700
On December 11th, 1995, residents of an oceanside community in San Francisco witnessed just how catastrophic a sewer collapse could be.

361
00:29:39,220 --> 00:29:46,080
There's a geyser of water coming out on a fancy street in San Francisco, and there's a tide of sewage flowing down past people's walls.

362
00:29:46,081 --> 00:29:51,320
This went on for 45 minutes until finally the sewer collapsed.

363
00:29:51,520 --> 00:29:52,220
It broke.

364
00:29:53,120 --> 00:29:58,340
It's like you've just got a machete and you just chopped through the garden hose.

365
00:29:58,800 --> 00:30:00,920
At that point, the water just goes glug, glug, glug.

366
00:30:01,460 --> 00:30:06,180
