367
00:30:11,200 --> 00:30:14,580
The sinkhole also damaged several nearby homes.

368
00:30:14,581 --> 00:30:19,580
The flow of heavy rains from the previous night was obstructed by a gate in the sewer line.

369
00:30:19,581 --> 00:30:25,580
The gate was being used to temporarily block sewage flow during construction on pipes downstream.

370
00:30:25,581 --> 00:30:30,580
We concluded that this gate had been left in a partly lowered position.

371
00:30:30,581 --> 00:30:34,580
So it's a bit like if you have a garden hose and the water is just flowing through it,

372
00:30:34,581 --> 00:30:38,580
and you put your foot on the garden hose, squeeze down on it,

373
00:30:38,581 --> 00:30:42,580
you pressurize the garden hose so that this gate created a pressure,

374
00:30:42,581 --> 00:30:48,340
pressure and the pressure was felt all the way up 1500 feet up the pressurized water needed

375
00:30:48,341 --> 00:30:53,940
another way out nearby sewer construction created a small sinkhole above the sewer line

376
00:30:55,300 --> 00:30:58,980
it grew during each rainfall creating a weak point over the tunnel

377
00:30:59,540 --> 00:31:02,740
and provided an ideal location for the water to break through

378
00:31:04,660 --> 00:31:10,580
san francisco sinkhole didn't injure anyone but a sinkhole in atlanta destroyed more than property

379
00:31:10,581 --> 00:31:18,340
In the early morning hours of June 14, 1993, just as a severe rainstorm was tapering off,

380
00:31:18,960 --> 00:31:24,220
two employees of the Marriott Courtyard Hotel in Atlanta, Georgia, were meeting in the hotel parking lot.

381
00:31:25,320 --> 00:31:27,960
Suddenly, the ground beneath them began to cave in.

382
00:31:28,720 --> 00:31:31,700
Within seconds, they were swept into a massive and watery chasm.

383
00:31:32,560 --> 00:31:38,140
They were innocent victims of a sewer collapse that resulted in an 80-foot-deep by 100-foot-wide sinkhole.

384
00:31:38,141 --> 00:31:43,100
Ensuing investigations delved into the 100-year history of the site

385
00:31:43,101 --> 00:31:45,780
and into the installation of a safety device

386
00:31:45,781 --> 00:31:49,060
that's very presence contributed to the sudden sinkhole formation.

387
00:31:51,460 --> 00:31:54,400
The sewer that collapsed, the Orange Street trunk sewer,

388
00:31:54,480 --> 00:31:57,020
was constructed in the early 1900s.

389
00:31:57,080 --> 00:32:00,560
It was an unreinforced concrete arch,

390
00:32:01,420 --> 00:32:05,260
and it was cutting edge for that particular time

391
00:32:05,261 --> 00:32:09,040
because prior to that, most of the sewers had been constructed of brick.

392
00:32:10,120 --> 00:32:14,900
Like many other sewer lines of the day, the Orm Street trunk was built above ground,

393
00:32:15,320 --> 00:32:20,200
simply a tube resting in a creek bed that utilized the natural slope of the stream.

394
00:32:21,080 --> 00:32:26,240
But during the 1960s, the tunnel was buried with fill from nearby freeway construction.

395
00:32:27,240 --> 00:32:28,900
Warehouses were then built over it.

396
00:32:28,901 --> 00:32:33,240
The condition that the improvements resulted in on that particular site

397
00:32:33,241 --> 00:32:40,180
raised that elevation to approximately 30 to 42 feet above the invert of the sewer.

398
00:32:40,960 --> 00:32:45,720
So it added a lot more weight above that structure

399
00:32:45,721 --> 00:32:50,040
than existed over it at any point during this previous history.

400
00:32:50,780 --> 00:32:54,580
In 1971, on the same site as the future Marriott parking lot,

401
00:32:54,780 --> 00:32:58,260
a 98-foot-wide sinkhole formed under a warehouse.

402
00:32:59,780 --> 00:33:01,200
The site was investigated.

403
00:33:01,201 --> 00:33:07,740
It was opened up, reconstructed, repaired, and no life was lost.

404
00:33:08,400 --> 00:33:11,880
In 1989, a hotel developer bought the neighboring lot.

405
00:33:13,060 --> 00:33:17,220
It was decided that the sewer line could support the hotel's surface parking lot.

406
00:33:18,580 --> 00:33:22,300
The design team, however, was concerned enough about the poor condition of the sewer

407
00:33:22,301 --> 00:33:25,200
that it researched safety devices for the site.

408
00:33:26,100 --> 00:33:29,900
A specialty contractor proposed a cost-effective and novel solution,

409
00:33:29,901 --> 00:33:35,700
burying an enormous geo-grid, or safety net, between the parking lot and the sewer.

410
00:33:36,400 --> 00:33:42,280
The geo-grid would alert people to a sinkhole by gradually sagging over an anticipated 20-foot wide void,

411
00:33:42,940 --> 00:33:47,420
suspending the parking lot for 100 hours, ample time to evacuate the area.

412
00:33:48,220 --> 00:33:51,240
But the ensuing sinkhole would overwhelm their estimates.

413
00:33:51,880 --> 00:33:59,360
Several days before the 1993 collapse, city workers inspected the sewer after reports of cracks in the hotel parking lot.

414
00:33:59,900 --> 00:34:03,660
At that point, one of the city inspectors actually walked part of the line,

415
00:34:04,500 --> 00:34:08,880
and they noticed that the invert upstream of the manhole,

416
00:34:09,140 --> 00:34:13,580
which is going toward the 1971 collapse zone, actually was heaved up.

417
00:34:13,960 --> 00:34:17,120
Two days later, before scheduled sewer repairs could be done,

418
00:34:17,720 --> 00:34:19,660
Atlanta was hit with a severe rainstorm.

419
00:34:20,340 --> 00:34:23,400
Cracks in the sewer walls allowed water to run outside of the sewer.

420
00:34:23,401 --> 00:34:27,420
The soil in the area was actually very silty,

421
00:34:27,421 --> 00:34:32,260
So it had a lot of very fine particles in it, and they're very susceptible to erosion.

422
00:34:32,740 --> 00:34:36,880
So if there is exfiltration, infiltration, those fine particles get picked up

423
00:34:36,881 --> 00:34:40,360
and then get reintroduced into the sewer and busy create these voids.

424
00:34:40,760 --> 00:34:47,200
What happened that day was that basically the sewer was carrying away a lot of the fines

425
00:34:47,201 --> 00:34:51,400
that the side walls could have collapsed at that point.

426
00:34:52,040 --> 00:34:56,480
So much of the supporting soil was washed away that the sewer gave way.

427
00:34:57,420 --> 00:35:01,840
The catastrophic sewer collapse resulted in a sinkhole that was 100 feet wide,

428
00:35:02,380 --> 00:35:04,640
five times the estimated 20-foot diameter.

429
00:35:05,700 --> 00:35:08,460
The geogrid supported the parking lot for five hours,

430
00:35:08,860 --> 00:35:12,120
but in doing so, concealed typical sinkhole warning signs.

431
00:35:12,680 --> 00:35:19,620
The early signs of distress were placed away from the center of what would later become the hole to the edges.

432
00:35:19,760 --> 00:35:24,540
The geogrid was pulling at anchor points, creating multiple small depressions,

433
00:35:24,541 --> 00:35:27,500
instead of one larger and more obvious one.

434
00:35:28,980 --> 00:35:33,420
Since the collapse, the sewer was replaced by new reinforced concrete pipe.

435
00:35:35,140 --> 00:35:38,740
These recent sewer collapses have been a warning to cities around the country

436
00:35:38,741 --> 00:35:41,240
that still depend on century-old sewers.

437
00:35:43,100 --> 00:35:44,780
Replacing sewer lines is costly,

438
00:35:45,320 --> 00:35:48,600
so strengthening existing pipes is a more practical solution.

439
00:35:48,601 --> 00:35:52,740
We've probably spent in the order of approximately $50 million

440
00:35:52,741 --> 00:35:56,445
dollars in making improvements to just the combined sewers.

441
00:35:56,446 --> 00:35:58,140
And we've done that using a

442
00:35:58,141 --> 00:36:01,413
rehabilitation process called Gunite.

443
00:36:01,414 --> 00:36:06,720
And Gunite is simply a concrete that can be sprayed onto the

444
00:36:06,721 --> 00:36:10,800
wall of the existing pipe. The Gunite strengthens sewer walls.

445
00:36:10,801 --> 00:36:12,840
But new technologies, including

446
00:36:12,841 --> 00:36:18,440
remote-controlled cameras which detect leaks and voids in and around sewers, are aiding cities in

447
00:36:18,441 --> 00:36:23,440
in the effort to catch failing sewers before they collapse and cause disaster.

