537
00:40:55,301 --> 00:41:02,900
the China's Yangtze River Delta experienced in 1931 when a system of levees also failed to hold

538
00:41:02,901 --> 00:41:04,521
back rushing waters.

539
00:41:04,522 --> 00:41:10,760
It burst through levees of with a wall of water about 22 feet high and caused

540
00:41:10,761 --> 00:41:18,500
3.7 million deaths it was the third largest flood on record it's the one that caused the most damage

541
00:41:18,501 --> 00:41:26,380
The Yenzi River basin is very large. The Yenzi River is about 6,300 kilometers long.

542
00:41:26,381 --> 00:41:33,060
And the basin have a very unique characteristics that is very high from the upstream region.

543
00:41:33,880 --> 00:41:42,740
The original source of the Yenzi River is from the Deepak-Qinghai Plateau, which has elevations 3,500 to 5,000 meters.

544
00:41:42,741 --> 00:41:48,520
then rushed down to the middle ridge about 2,000 to 500 meters high

545
00:41:48,521 --> 00:41:53,740
and then to the flatter area downstream and then empty into the sea at Shanghai.

546
00:41:54,640 --> 00:41:58,880
Due to the powerful flow of the river, called the Dragon by the Chinese,

547
00:41:59,760 --> 00:42:03,560
great floods historically raged through this area about every 10 years.

548
00:42:04,400 --> 00:42:05,860
There's two major reasons.

549
00:42:05,861 --> 00:42:09,560
One is the high plateau in the upstream reaches.

550
00:42:09,561 --> 00:42:16,780
and they concentrate the rainfall very quickly to the downstream, the middle and lower reaches.

551
00:42:17,420 --> 00:42:22,860
The other reason is a lot of moist caused storms gathered from the Bay of Bengal

552
00:42:22,861 --> 00:42:28,880
and the Indian Ocean come to the high mountains, and that produced enormous flood.

553
00:42:30,200 --> 00:42:34,940
The main flood protection in this area was provided by a system of makeshift levees

554
00:42:34,941 --> 00:42:37,740
built by the generations of farmers who lived there.

555
00:42:39,560 --> 00:42:44,980
The levees are built along the banks of rivers, so they're built up in layers.

556
00:42:45,420 --> 00:42:50,140
Back in the 1800s, these would probably be compacted with animals.

557
00:42:50,780 --> 00:42:57,400
So there's levees around that are hundreds of years old that are very susceptible to high water erosion,

558
00:42:58,520 --> 00:43:03,000
earthquakes, water overtopping them, and you have these failures.

559
00:43:03,001 --> 00:43:10,000
While the Chinese were threatened by an imminent Japanese invasion in the summer of 1931, a

560
00:43:10,001 --> 00:43:15,000
series of very heavy storms passed through this region, when there should have only been

561
00:43:15,001 --> 00:43:16,000
two.

562
00:43:16,001 --> 00:43:21,000
This is a perfect storm situation where the right meteorological conditions occurred,

563
00:43:21,001 --> 00:43:29,000
where storms sat over the river basin for a long time period, and then it just overwhelms

564
00:43:29,001 --> 00:43:32,540
overwhelms the system that's designed to contain them.

565
00:43:33,420 --> 00:43:36,380
Deng Ting Lake was flanked by some of China's oldest levees.

566
00:43:37,100 --> 00:43:40,620
The lowlands that surround it are just 105 feet above sea level.

567
00:43:41,300 --> 00:43:45,020
When the levees failed, Deng Ting became a vast inland sea.

568
00:43:46,140 --> 00:43:51,660
It's like a wall of water in the height of a two-story building coming through.

569
00:43:51,940 --> 00:43:55,360
And when that happens, of course, the roads are very upstream and downstream.

570
00:43:55,361 --> 00:44:01,840
The waters rose above the rooftops of homes and large population centers, including Nanking and Wuhan.

571
00:44:02,440 --> 00:44:07,840
And 51 million people, one-fourth of China's population at the time, became homeless.

572
00:44:09,080 --> 00:44:10,240
They were the lucky ones.

573
00:44:10,920 --> 00:44:14,740
Approximately 145,000 people were killed by the flood itself,

574
00:44:15,140 --> 00:44:20,620
while millions of others suffered later deaths due to disease and starvation caused by the disaster.

575
00:44:21,240 --> 00:44:24,760
The area near Wuhan remained flooded for more than four months.

576
00:44:25,360 --> 00:44:29,680
the depth of the water exceeding six feet and in places more than 20 feet.

577
00:44:30,540 --> 00:44:34,960
With the country now at war with Japan, recovering from the disaster was difficult,

578
00:44:35,740 --> 00:44:39,980
and maintaining and building a stronger infrastructure was not an immediate priority.

579
00:44:41,560 --> 00:44:44,740
Since 1931, there's another war.

580
00:44:44,741 --> 00:44:52,300
The Japanese invasion is 1937 to 1945, and then there's a civil war, 1945 to 1949.

581
00:44:52,301 --> 00:44:59,100
So after 1949, the current government has done quite a bit to control the flood.

582
00:44:59,780 --> 00:45:04,580
And they have established local river basins and they upgrade the major levees.

583
00:45:05,180 --> 00:45:10,200
In 1992, they also began constructing the Three Gorges Dam,

584
00:45:10,940 --> 00:45:18,020
a controversial dam that rises 600 feet into the sky and stretches 1.5 miles across the river.

585
00:45:18,840 --> 00:45:21,440
It's due to be completed in 2009.

586
00:45:21,441 --> 00:45:27,480
The Three Gorges Dam has so much flood carrying capacity.

587
00:45:27,980 --> 00:45:30,480
It's about 21 billion cubic meters.

588
00:45:31,420 --> 00:45:34,520
For example, the 1931 flood happens again.

